@node PART_01 "Introduction"

A saw a lot of LastCaller doors and scripts, but I always though
'huh, I could do this better!'. Thats why I wrote this door.Nowadays
it is a SIM module, coz I had to scan the CallersLog in Node(1) and
I had also running some statistics.

@endnode

@node PART_02 "Requirements"

What U need to run it...
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++

 - the installed /X-Software (V3.20++)

Now let's go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...

@endnode

@node PART_03 "Installation for MDB-LastCallers 3.00"

How to install it to your /X-System...
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

First make a Drawer into Doors: called 'MDB-LastCallers' and copy the Files
 - 'MDB-LASTCALLERS'
 - 'MDB-LASTCALLERS.INFO'
 - 'FOOTER.TXT'
 - 'HEADER.TXT'
into it.

Second copy the Icon 'LOGOFF1.INFO' into the SYSCmd Drawer.

@endnode

@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for MDB-LastCallers 3.00"

                                ToolTypes
                                ~~~~~~~~~

                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-LASTCALLERS 3.00" LINK PART_04_LC}

                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR LOGOFF<n>           " LINK PART_04_LO}

                    @{" THE LOGOFF SCRIPT                 " LINK PART_04_SC}

@endnode

@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-LastCallers 3.00

                 ToolTypes for MDB-LastCallers 3.00
                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

BULL=<filename>                 - This ToolType specifies the output-file.
                                  /X calls this one a BULL. Include this
                                  in your login-Bull so that every caller
                                  sees the last 10 callers.
                                  Eg. BULL=BBS:LastCallers.txt

HEADER=<filename>               - The header tooltype specifies which file
                                  will be joined before the LastCallers info.
                                  Eg. FOOTER=Doors:MDB-LastCallers/Header.txt

FOOTER=<filename>               - The footer tooltype specifies which file
                                  will be joined behind the LastCallers info.
                                  Eg. FOOTER=Doors:MDB-LastCallers/Footer.txt

CALLERSLOG=<filename>           - This tooltypes indicates which log must be
                                  be scanned.
                                  Eg. CALLERSLOG=BBS:Node1/CallersLog

DATA=<filename>                 - The data tooltype specifies where the
                                  datafile is stored. This file is needed
                                  everytime. If it doesn't exists, the door
                                  will create this file itself.
                                  Eg. FOOTER=Doors:MDB-LastCallers/Footer.txt


@endnode

@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For LogOff<x>"

                       ToolTypes for LogOff<x>"
                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

As noted in Chapter @{"Introduction" LINK PART_01}, this Door is a SIM
module. The script must be called when a user is signing off, e.g. if
he/she is running in node 1, then you must have 'LOGOFF1.INFO' in your
SYSCmd Drawer.

LOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the script
                                  is located.
                                  Eg. LOCATION=BBS:Node1/Logoff.script

MULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may
                                  started in different nodes.
                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES

PRIORITY=<n>                    - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos
                                  priority when the Door is executed.
                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2

STACK=<n>                       - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.
                                  Eg. STACK=8096

TYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.
                                  This Door is a script so TYPE=SIM

@endnode

@node PART_04_SC "The LogOff script"

The script file is needed, coz here you can tell which batch jobs you want
to run. In this case you are only interested in the last callers, so you
make in file LOGOFF.SCRIPT in your NODE<num> Drawer. It look likes the
following example:

^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^CUT HERE ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Doors:MDB-LastCallers/MDB-LastCallers
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^CUT HERE ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

And then you have to change the attribute bytes of this script:
 SET THE S BIT FOR SCRIPT with Dopus or with C:PROTECT
DO NOT FORGET THIS ONE, ELSE IT WON'T WORK!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

@endnode

@node PART_05 "Changes"

3.00 (12-Jun-1994)
    - Totally changed!
    - The bull that will be created, looks different; more info is shown.
    - Only the actual lastcaller will be recorded in the bull, thats why
      I added the DATA-TOOLTYPE.

2.00 (11-Jun-1994(
    - Never released! Ha Ha Ha

1.7  (06-Jun-1994)
  - Searcher improved, now scans for 60 '*' for the starting
    of a user!

1.6  (03-Jun-1994)
  - Some coding enhanced.

0.05 (05- Mrt-1994)
 - SIM module instead of real XIM.

0.04 (27-Feb-1994)
 - Icon based.

0.03 (??-????-1994)
 - Should run on all processors now.

@endnode

